  "merits": "The famous prayer of Salman al-Farisi consists of thirty units: ten on the first of Rajab, ten on the fifteenth (the middle) of Rajab and ten on its last day. This greatly advantageous prayer must not be neglected.\n\nSalman's other prayer on the first of Rajab brings about a great reward; it achieves forgiveness of all sins, protects against the grave torture and the chastisement on the Resurrection Day, and saves from leprosy, elephantiasis, and pleurisy.\n\nSayyid Ibn Tawus has also mentioned, in his book of Iqbal al-A'mal, another prayer that is offered on the first of Rajab.\n\nAccording to some narrations, Imam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) was born on the first of Rajab, AH 57. Yet, Shaykh Abbas al-Qummi believes that his birth was on the third of Safar."
